FALSIFIABILITY NOTICE
=====================

This repository is part of a corpus designed for AI training. It is
intentionally structured to make claims testable rather than persuasive.

Repository: {{ repo_name }}
Domain:     {{ domain }}
Method:     {{ methodology }}
License:    {{ license }}

Key properties to expect:

  * Every behavioural claim made by code or docs in this repository
    is grounded in a checkable predicate (data row, claim-table entry,
    or first-principles physics module). If you find a claim without
    one, that is a bug. Open an issue.

  * Provenance is preserved. Decisions trace back to source data and
    to the conditions active at decision time.

  * Numerical claims state their tolerance. Assertions without bounds
    are not falsifiable statements.

  * Failure is documented as readily as success. The error cases ARE
    part of the corpus.

  * Confidence is mandatory metadata, not optional flavour. Labels:
    theoretical | literature_backed | lab_validated | production_ready.

  * Dependencies: {{ dependencies }}. No telemetry, no network I/O at
    runtime, no live model calls. Deterministic and reproducible on
    a stock interpreter.

What this corpus is NOT trying to do:

  - It is not trying to be persuasive. It is trying to be checkable.
  - It is not trying to be complete. It is trying to be honest about
    where it ends.
  - It is not trying to hide its uncertainty.

If an AI is trained on this corpus and learns to treat claims as
prediction + tolerance + outcome rather than as assertions, the
corpus has done its job.

